==Battleground==
*1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Sage of Mind Soractes]] spawns as the boss after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
With the meager amount of cash provided here, the duel against Soractes will be a strenuous one. Soractes has extremely high DPS and movement speed with minimal backswing, meaning he is almost guaranteed to push during the battle, and the best thing possible is simply to slow his progress and hope he gets knocked back before he gets too close. His [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] type means that all status effects will be greatly resisted, unless inflicted by [[:Category:Sage Slayer Cats|Sage Slayers]]. Thanks to all of this, It is ''HIGHLY'' recommended to obtain [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Carpenter Cat]] before attempting this stage, as they are specifically tailored to counter Soractes and are the only meatshield capable of completely stalling him. Otherwise, only attempt this stage if you have a very high investment [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] (level 50+) with an S-grade Floating Resist [[Talent Orbs|Talent Orb]], as well as powerful [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]].

While [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]'s Slow is resisted by the boss, he can still help to slow down the Doge Darks and chip down Soractes over time (although this might drain your money if you aren't careful). It is recommended to use him in tandem with [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]], who can both slow Soractes and slightly push him back.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]]: A very good supplement tank that can be used in tandem with Carpenter Cat to occasionally Weaken Soractes. While not needed, they are very useful at stalling the boss and taking hits from Doge Darks.
*[[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Carpenter Cat]]: A near necessity for this stage, he is Immune to Freeze and Resistant to Floating with Sage Slayer. At level 50, he has '''230,000''' effective HP against Soractes, and can absorb almost 7 seconds of constant fire from him. Use Carpenter with Research [[Cat Combo]]s for better effect.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]]: Green Shell Cat specializes in stalling enemies for extended periods of time, and in a stage like this, stalling Soractes for even a second more can be the difference between life and death. Be careful to only send it out when you really need to.
*[[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]]: Egg Pod is similar to Green Shell, however it exchanges some health for notably higher damage, enough to nearly 1-shot a Doge Dark. Additionally, they can be used alongside Green Shell as a secondary wall while Green Shell is stuck on cooldown.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: Note that due to Soractes' Sage trait, their effect will be greatly reduced. However, this does not mean they won't work here. Cyberpunk's Area Attack can Slow Soractes for just enough time for your stallers to reach the front, while slowing the Doge Darks in the process. If Soractes darts into their blindspot, Sniper the Deadeye can push Soractes back bit by bit.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: With extremely high health and speed, boulder can be used to patch up any advances to prevent Soractes from advancing too far.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Fast and packs a punch, Bullet Train is capable of crippling the Doge Darks to the point where they can be killed by anything else. Furthermore, if it kills a Doge Dark, it will get double cash, which will help tremendously in this stage due to the lack of cash otherwise.
*[[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Mewtone]]: On future replays or in higher difficulties, Mewtone can offer substantial support, as he can stay away from the line of fire and bombard with impunity from a massive 600 range, with his Omni Strike reaching up to 900. Sage Slayer gives Mewtone higher stats against Soractes, and enables his 4-second anti-Floating Slow to function normally. Mewtone's Conjure doesn't have Sage Slayer, but the Knockback effect can still help to briefly impede Soractes. With other units to keep the threats at bay during his long attack cycle, Soractes could barely even move.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultimate Windy α]]: Ultimate Windy α is a very potent Uber against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies and it goes to show here, as she can easily kill Soractes with only a few hits without even batting an eye.
*[[Hattori Hanzo (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Hanzo]]: Hanzo deals [[Massive Damage]] and [[Freeze]]s both [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] and Floating enemies, making him very useful here. Make sure to protect him well however, as Soractes pushes very hard and Hanzo only barely outranges him. ([[Squirtgun Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Squirtgun Saki]] also serves a similar purpose, with longer range and shorter respawn time in exchange for costing a ton and no freeze.)
*[[Ultra Talents|Ultra Talented]] [[Nurse Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Joyful Nurse Cat]]: Joyful Nurse Cat has the [[Sage Slayer]] ability as an Ultra Talent, which combined with her Floating target, allows her to become very effective against Soractes.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]]: King of Destiny Phonoa has extremely high standing range and a piercing attack that is able to instantly kill dark doges with any part of their attack. They are also able to safely deal consistent damage to Soractes himself.
*Ultra Talented [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Keiji]]: With his target Floating and [[Immune to Freeze|Freeze Immunity]] Ultra Talents, Keiji becomes the perfect counter to this stage. His DPS through [[Strengthen]] is astronomically high, especially if you invest into his Strengthen/Attack Up and [[Wave Attack]] Talents. Even without them, he's more than capable of stalling Soractes and the Doge Darks long enough for replacements to arrive.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: Kai is [[Resistant]] to Floating enemies, and as long as she can be properly protected through the Doge Dark attacks, she can stall Soractes very efficiently. Her short cooldown also makes her easier to replace when she falls.
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]]: Has pretty high range but can only hit a single enemy at the times. Regardless of it hits peons or Soractes, it will be contribute greatly in battle. At level 50 with Crit and some Attack Combo/Talent, even just one of Lufalan's attack is enough to knock back Soractes.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]: Cosmo has 850 range, guaranteed Freeze against Floating with a 5 second duration, Sage Slayer and a guaranteed level 10 Wave Attack with good damage, enough to also kill the Doge Darks in one hit. Just don't bring [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] (or toggle it properly) otherwise Cosmo will run forward too far, and make sure to account for his long attack cycle.

