==Trivia==
*Adherence to Virtue may refer to [[wikipedia:Virtue ethics|virtue ethics]], an ethical theory that has its roots in ancient Greece with [[wikipedia:Socrates|Socrates]], who believed virtue is equivalent to knowledge.
*As the final stage of [[Garden of Wilted Thoughts]], Adherence to Virtue is the 48th and last [[Zero Legends]] stage to take place in a [[Media:Map040.png|jumbled up and mirrored Japan]], the 1st being [[Crimes Against the Cosmos]]. This parallels how the [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapters]] have 48 stages each, ending with a unique boss and reward.
**These 48 stages may specifically represent the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]] of [[Empire of Cats]], which takes place across the 47 prefectures of Japan and [[wikipedia:Iriomote Island|Iriomote Island]] rather than various countries and the [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]].
**Despite being the last of these stages, Adherence to Virtue has several parallels to Empire of Cats stage 1, [[Korea (Empire of Cats)|Korea/Nagasaki]]:
***Korea/Nagasaki uses the day overworld background, while Adherence to Virtue uses the night overworld background (with [[A Whole New World]]'s background mixed in).
***Korea/Nagasaki spawns a single [[Doge]] at the start of the [[battle]], then spawns Doges infinitely, while Adherence to Virtue does the same with [[Doge Dark]]s.
***Not counting [[Ms. Sign]], the only enemy in Korea/Nagasaki is Doge, while Adherence to Virtue only has Doge Dark and [[Sage of Mind Soractes]], whose Japanese description implies that his encounter with the Cat Army was unplanned. Soractes is also seen emerging from a wormhole rather than a typical enemy base, although the same could be said for the Doge Darks.
***Adherence to Virtue's [https://youtu.be/_KhgY0ArzW4 battle theme] contains the leitmotif of "[https://youtu.be/bxfOwm4OeiQ Nihon Shinryaku!]" (日本侵略, "Invading Japan!"), which first plays in Korea/Nagasaki. A comparison can be found [https://youtu.be/_PgaLrxla0c?si=HUnGVYxPwzZFKZtd here].
*Adherence to Virtue has a unique "Defeated..." message: "Soractes is a [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] enemy that is resistant to debuffs! Any [[:Category:Sage Slayer Cats|unit with the Sage Slayer ability]] can negate his resistance to debuffs!"
*Adherence to Virtue appears to have been designed specifically for [[Nurse Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Joyful Nurse Cat]], whose Ultra [[Talents]] were added in [[Version 13.1 Update|Version 13.1]] alongside Garden of Wilted Thoughts. Joyful Nurse Cat can knockback and slow both traits in the stage, and her Sage Slayer Ultra Talent improves her performance against Sage of Mind Soractes.
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Soractes]] had a 3% drop chance from this stage.

